# Grant user pi ownership of the LCD backlight brightness sysfs file so the
# dsky HMI (running as pi) can turn the screen off/on for its screensaver.
# The panel is an i2c client on bus 10 at address 0x45; that kernel name is
# stable across reboots.
#
# A plain OWNER="pi" does NOT work here: the backlight class device has no
# devnode (its devpath is a sysfs directory under platform/soc/...i2c-10),
# and this udev (systemd 247) applies rule ownership only to devnodes, not
# to attribute files of directory devices. RUN+= runs as root during the add
# event, so the chown always succeeds.
SUBSYSTEM=="backlight", KERNEL=="10-0045", RUN+="/bin/chown pi /sys/class/backlight/10-0045/brightness"
